triage:c5_qa3_REQ_C5_008 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "REQ-C5-008" ;
 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "open" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "05e4c8cf0c2c7740f4f0a3ff71a7ee1f98e5c2ba" ;
 triage:file "tests/unit/generation/test_monty_example.py:137; tests/unit/generation/test_monty_example.py:150; scripts/new_project.py:159; scripts/new_project.py:227" ;
 triage:issue "The new planted-Cargo.lock regression fixes the intended inventory assertion but calls generation.cargo_generate directly inside the unittest. That executes both the cargo-generate version probe and generation command through subprocess.run with captured stdout/stderr and no deadline or owned process-tree cleanup. A hung cargo/plugin/hook or inherited pipe writer can therefore hang this new test indefinitely; the successful current run does not satisfy the binding bounded-ownership validation policy." ;
 triage:action "Keep the planted stale-lock fixture and absence assertion, but execute its generation through the canonical bounded owned-process boundary (or adapt every invoked external process to that existing owner). Preserve physical descendant cleanup and regular-file capture on errors/timeouts, with a causal stalled-generation negative. Do not rewrite the product driver broadly, weaken byte preservation, skip, retry or extend timing windows. Reuse the same narrow fix for the C2/C3 copied regression as needed." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6676408599" .

